-- title:
--   Pole-chart sections read as coefficient embeddings of q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a witness $hj$ that the Laurent series $j(q)$, namely `jqModC ℚ`, lies in $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the integral form ratios at full level. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an element of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the structure packaging a two-chart integral model $X$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(M)$ over `R p`, proper, flat, integral and locally of finite presentation with integrally closed affine sections, the corresponding $\Gamma_N$-level model proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$, a curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, an isomorphism $\eta = \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ from $\mathrm{Meta}.C$ onto the base change $X \times_{\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathrm{R}\,p} \mathrm{Spec}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over the base, Galois equivariance of the induced bijection on places, and the finite-chart case of the present identity. Let $b$ be an element of `chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj`, the subalgebra of the function field generated over `R p` by $j^{-1}$. Then the open subscheme of $\mathrm{Meta}.C$ obtained by pulling back the image of the pole chart $\iota_\infty$ along $\eta$ followed by the first projection is non-empty, and the following holds: transport $b$ to a section of $X$ over $\iota_\infty(\top)$ (through the canonical identifications of $\Gamma(\mathrm{Spec})$ and of the chart immersion), pull it back along $\eta$ followed by the first projection, take its germ in the function field of $\mathrm{Meta}.C$, and carry it back through $\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ into `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`; the resulting element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ equals `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` applied to the $q$-expansion of $b$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, i.e. its coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the pole-chart ($j^{-1}$) counterpart of the field `Meta_pin` of the Deligne–Rapoport model structure, which records the same dictionary for the finite chart: on the geometric generic fibre, chart functions are read through the curve model's function-field identification as the coefficient embedding of their $q$-expansions. It is used in the study of the model's cusps, of valuations of chart elements, and in the Atkin–Lehner comparisons on the generic fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_coe_ffEquiv_symm_germToFunctionField_app_iotaInf_eq_coeffEmb.lean

